  "prefLabel": "Plc 1802.21 Full statistical revaluation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1802.21 “Full statistical revaluation” means the process of a revaluation of all taxable and nontaxable properties in a municipality, using existing property data, to arrive at full and true value as of April 1st. The term includes “statistical update” and “statistical reassessment.”\n\nSource. #14330, eff 9-22-25, EXPIRES: 9-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1800.html"
